Judge Reason: The HALLUCINATION score is not perfect because the answer contains minor generalizations not directly supported by the research data.
Output:
An AI agent is a software program that uses artificial intelligence to interact with its environment, collect data, and perform self-directed tasks to achieve predetermined goals set by humans. It has the ability to independently choose the best actions to meet those goals and can extend its capabilities by connecting to external software, APIs, or devices. This allows AI agents to perform a wide range of tasks, from retrieving data and sending emails to controlling hardware and running code. 

The agent works by receiving a specific instruction or goal from the user, planning tasks to achieve that goal, breaking down the goal into smaller actionable tasks, and then performing those tasks based on specific orders or conditions. AI agents can also learn and adapt over time, and they can work with other agents to coordinate and perform more complex workflows. 

In essence, an AI agent is a system that uses a large language model to decide the control flow of an application, and its level of autonomy and ability to make decisions can vary depending on how much control flow the model owns. AI agents can be designed as applications or products, such as AI assistants, to collaborate directly with users and perform tasks by understanding and responding to natural human language and inputs.
